<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;</font></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">C.01.06 ChemStation with =
GC/G1888: last run completes but the ChemStation remains in the run state</=
font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">OpenLAB CDS ChemStation E=
dition C.01.06 with a G1888 sequence never finishes.  The last vial complet=
es but the sequence continues to be in the run state and must be stopped ma=
nually.  Once stop has been selected, allow time for the system to process =
and cleanup.  Try to avoid using abort.
=20
Use of ABORT almost immediately terminates all ChemStation activities and p=
rocesses. This has the potential to leave any currently running sequence in=
 a strange state. Also any consecutive Data Analysis is aborted. When the C=
hemStation is connected to central storage (OpenLAB ECM or OpenLAB Data Sto=
re), no files will be uploaded to the repository after aborting the sequenc=
e. Loss of data may occur.
After using the Abort function, close and restart the ChemStation Applicati=
on.
=20
Always try STOP first and allow enough time for consecutive processing and =
cleanup.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">n/a</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This problem is addressed=
 with Integrated Headspace Software revision B.01.06.</font></pre><p></p>




