</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Addition of new columns t=
o the column catalog (database) is not possible after upgrade</font></pre><=
p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Upgrading from B.01.03 to=
 B.04.02, it is no longer possible to add new columns to the GC column cata=
log (database) in Rev. B.04.02.

The following error is shown:

The Catalog File cannot be opened.  If needed, you may obtain an appropriat=
e replacement file from Agilent.
C:\Chem32\CORE\...\DRIVERS\catalog.mdb</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">The problem is that there=
 are several columns that have the same manufacturer and model number. Our =
new database software doesn=E2=80=99t handle this.

The newer database software (in B.04.02 for example) no longer allows dupli=
cates of manufacturer + model number. i.e., there can only be one HP HP-5 i=
n the database.  Note: the new software will inform the user that the model=
 number =E2=80=9Cxxx=E2=80=9D is already in use and request that a differen=
t value be chosen. (The user is returned to the original entry screen with =
all the info filled in.)=20

In theory, customers should not be creating more than one catalog entry wit=
h the same model number.  It=E2=80=99s like having two items in the LLBean =
catalog with the same order number!  But, of course, the older software all=
owed the duplicates.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Before upgrading, fix the=
 problem with the column database duplicates while running B.01.03 for exam=
ple.  Review the column catalogs and make sure there are no duplicates and =
fix any that exist before the upgrade.</font></pre><p></p>




