<a id=3D"#TTID:" 470764=3D"" name=3D"TTID:470764"></a>
<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:470764&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:OpenLAB CDS ChemS=
tation Edition&nbsp;&nbsp;M83xx&nbsp;&nbsp;C.01.10 Update 3</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Installation</fon=
t></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">For disabling TLS 1.0 on =
AIC's with Server 2016, SQL with high availability DB is needed</font></pre=
><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">On an AIC on Windows 2016=
 Server, if TLS 1.0 gets disabled, it is not possible to launch/configure i=
nstruments on AIC or client and AIC software throws exceptions.=20
Note: This would not be observed on an OS Windows 2019 server.</font></pre>=
<p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">As a workaround it is pos=
sible to install Microsoft SQL Express with Management Studio in Windows au=
thentication mode, and do some configuration steps of SQL and the RDS servi=
ce.=20
Add the "NT AUTHORITY\NETWORK SERVICE" to the SQL Server administrators and=
 give it later the server role "dbcreator" with Management Studio. Create a=
 folder for the database and give "NT AUTHORITY\NETWORK SERVICE" full contr=
ol.
Enable TCP/IP for the SQL instance and configure port 1433 for IPALL.=20
In the Server Manager navigate to Remote Desktop Services/Overview. Right c=
lick on RD Connection Broker and select "Configure High Availability". Unde=
r configuration type select "Dedicated database server". In the configurati=
on the qualified DNS name, connection string and the database folder mentio=
ned above.=20
Then the IISCrypto tool can be used to unconfigure TLS 1.0 and TLS 1.1 and =
keep TLS 1.2 configured. Restart to apply the settings. </font></pre><p></p=
>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">There is no fix from Chem=
Station side possible.  Microsoft Windows Server 2016 OS does not come with=
 an identification database ( called WID )
which supports TLS1.2</font></pre><p></p>




<hr>
