Station Edition&nbsp;&nbsp;M83xx&nbsp;&nbsp;C.01.10,LTS 01.11</font></b><br=
>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Programming</font=
></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">The "Turn Lamps Off" post=
 sequence macro also turns off RID temperature</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">In the Sequence Parameter=
s under the Shutdown section, the "Turn Lamps Off" post-sequence macro also=
 disables the RID temperature control. However, turning off the RID tempera=
ture is not recommended, as it requires a significant amount of time to re-=
equilibrate during the next startup.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">To avoid turning off the =
RID heater, create a custom post-sequence command that only switches off th=
e DAD lamp:

retval$=3DSendModule$(DAD1, "LAMP 0")

Steps to Implement:
1.	Open Sequence Parameters from the Sequence menu.
2.	Under Post-Sequence Command/Macro, select Set Custom Command Template fr=
om the dropdown.
3.	Click Add to create a new custom command.
4.	Paste the command above into the script editor and save.
5.	Once saved, the new command will appear in the Post-Sequence Command/Mac=
ro dropdown. Select it to apply.

</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
