<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:1284298&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:OpenLAB CDS Chem=
Station Edition&nbsp;&nbsp;M83xx&nbsp;&nbsp;C.01.10,LTS 01.11</font></b><br=
>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Programming</font=
></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">ChemStation startup failu=
re with blank user interface after installation of Microsoft Windows update=
s</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">OpenLab ChemStation fails=
 to start because the CTL3D32.DLL is missing. This DLL was removed by the i=
nstallation of Microsoft Windows update(s):

Microsoft Windows 11 Updates:
=E2=80=A2	KB5065426 (OS Build 26100.6584) released September 9, 2025
=E2=80=A2	KB5064081 (OS Build 26100.5074) Preview released August 29, 2025

After applying these updates, ChemStation fails to launch and displays a bl=
ank user interface.=20
</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">There are 2 workarounds:

1.	Uninstall the Windows Update(s):

a)	Open Settings &gt; Windows Update &gt; Update History
b)	Select Uninstall Updates
c)	Locate KB5064081 and KB5065426 or KB5065429 and select Uninstall

2.	Put back the DLL

a)	Look for the CTL3D32.DLL on your computer, you may have a copy of it und=
er the path C:\Windows\WinSxS\x86_microsoft-windows-ctl3d32_xyz =20

Example:  "C:\Windows\WinSxS\x86_microsoft-windows-ctl3d32_31bf3856ad364e35=
_10.0.22621.1_none_cfa016988f815eda\ctl3d32.dll"

If you do not have the DLL on your computer, try to get it from a different=
 computer.
Avoid downloading from third-party sites, as these may pose security risks.

b)	Copy the DLL to C:\Windows\SysWOW64=20
No need to register the DLL.

Note: Agilent cannot distribute Microsoft-owned system files such as CTL3D3=
2.DLL. =20
The DLL is not available from Microsoft and must be sourced from a working =
PC.

Follow-up communication will be provided once a resolution is available.
</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">n/a</font></pre><p></p>




<hr>
