eporting&nbsp;&nbsp;OpenLAB Intelligent Reporting&nbsp;&nbsp;A.01.07</font>=
</b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Report Templates<=
/font></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Min and Max column summar=
y calculations report GMT and not local time for date fields</font></pre><p=
></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Times stamps reported as =
part of a summary calculation, e.g. minimum or maximum of all time stamps i=
n a table column, are reported in GMT time rather than your local time. The=
 column values are reported in local time.

This defect is caused by a missing SYSTEM.TIMEZONE.CURRENTTIMEZONE.TOLOCALT=
IME(...) conversion in the .rdl template file.</font></pre><p></p>
