<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Data acquired with OpenLa=
b CDS ChemStation Edition C.01.06 and higher may show an ambiguous date for=
matting for the calibration curve modification time stamp using intelligent=
 reports. Day and month are switched. It only affects long and short date f=
ormats set as: "dd-MM-yyyy".=20

1.) If the day is between 1st and 12th AND if system's long date format is =
set as "dd-MM-yyyy" an incorrect calibration modified date will be seen in =
the report generated as part of sequence run as well on reprocessing the se=
quence.

2.) If the day is between 1st and 12th AND if system's Short date format is=
 set as "dd-MM-yyyy" an incorrect calibration modified date will be seen in=
 the report generated from DA view -&gt; Print report=20

Other time stamps are not affected. </font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
