</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Bouncing menu</font></pre=
><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This happens only if the =
user manually configures a thermostat along to his already set up sampler i=
n the LC stack.
In this case the revision, serial number and type of the thermostat is not =
properly propagated to the internal configuration within the LC driver duri=
ng the DownloadConfigSettings call.
That caused a ping pong situation where the CDS sends the complete configur=
ation to the driver which detects the differences due to the incorrect inte=
rnal configuration propagation and therefore triggers a new configchanged e=
vent.=20
To fix this issue, the driver needs to propagate the serial number, revisio=
n and type of the manual configured thermostat to the actual configuration =
after a DownloadConfigSettings.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">n/a</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">OpenLAB CDS ChemStation E=
dition - SP2 for LC RC.Net Driver A.02.05 and A.02.06</font></pre><p></p>




