<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">While running registerCS.=
bat, no registration in OpenLAB Shared Services will happen.=20

You will receive following message in command prompt: =E2=80=98C:\Program=
=E2=80=99 is not recognized as an internal or external command, operable pr=
ogram or batch file.

The reason for this behavior is that the new installation path for the Chem=
Station now contains spaces=20
C:\Program Files (x86)=20
which was not the case before=20
C:\Chem32
</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">To fix this issue, you ha=
ve to modify registerCS.bat manually.=20

Use Notepad to edit the RegisterCS.bat file.=20

1.   On computers with User Access Control enabled, you will need to open N=
otepad as an Administrator by right-clicking on the Notepad program and sel=
ect Run as Administrator. =20


If you do not Run as Administrator, you will not be able to save your chang=
es.

2.     From Notepad, navigate to the RegisterCS.bat file found under C:\Pro=
gram Files (x86)\Agilent Technologies\ChemStation\CORE.

3.     Edit the last line by adding two quotation mark characters ( =E2=80=
=9C ) as in the example below:=20
=20
Change     %~dp0\RegisterCSData.exe     to    "%~dp0\RegisterCSData.exe"
=20
The last line appears like this:
"%~dp0\RegisterCSData.exe" /URL=3D%LOGON_URL% /User=3D%LOGON_USER% /Passwor=
d=3D%LOGON_PASSWORD% /Add %AIC_MODE%
=20
4.     Save RegisterCS.bat file. =20

5.     Run the registerCS.bat file to register the new PC name.
</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Resolved in OpenLab CDS C=
hemStation C.01.08 Update 1.</font></pre><p></p>




